# Reference: <https://postmarketos.org/vendorkernel>
# Kernel: bengris32/linux-mtk (mainline-based MT8163 kernel), branch mt8163/7.0,
# pinned to commit $_commit below, plus the patches and the MT6625L driver
# tarball in source=. See NOTICE for where each part comes from.

maintainer="liamtw22 <31185529+liamtw22@users.noreply.github.com>"
pkgname=linux-amazon-biscuit
# pkgver tracks what this source actually builds, which is NOT 6.6.30.
# bengris32/linux-mtk branch mt8163/7.0 is a 7.0-rc kernel: the built modules
# install under /lib/modules/7.0.0-rc6 and `uname -r` reports 7.0.0-rc6. The
# 6.6.30 carried here until 2026-09-04 was simply wrong - harmless while this
# was a private tree, misleading the moment anyone else installs it.
#
# _rc6 is apk's release-candidate suffix, so this sorts after 6.6.30 (7 > 6)
# and before a future 7.0.0 release. pkgrel is NOT reset to 0 on this change:
# r229 had not been built yet, and the project's docs number kernels by pkgrel,
# so restarting the count would break every reference for no gain.
pkgver=7.0.0_rc6
pkgrel=243
install="$pkgname.pre-install $pkgname.pre-upgrade"
pkgdesc="Amazon Echo Dot (2nd gen) mainline kernel fork"
arch="aarch64"
